 ## Background
-The Aggregated Bidirectional Scattering Distribution Function (ABSDF) method was presented in the paper "Efficient Scene Appearance Aggregation for Level-of-Detail Rendering" by Yang Zhou, Tao Huang, Ravi Ramamoorthi, Pradeep Sen, and Ling-Qi Yan, published in October 2024 [S1, unofficial]. The method addresses the challenge of rendering large, complex scenes with high geometric detail by aggregating the appearance of surfaces within a volume into a compact representation. It builds upon previous work in appearance aggregation and LoD rendering, aiming to provide a scalable solution for physically based rendering of massive scenes [S1, unofficial].
